But Mariammes children did euerie day stomacke the matter more and more, disdaining to giue place vnto their inferiour: and for their nobiltie not enduring to be remoued from their places and not to keepe their dignitie also: their wiues did the like, and Alexanders wife Glaphyra, 
                         who was the daughter of Archelaus king of Cappadocia, did greatly enuy and disdaine Salome; 
