And this (quoth he) is the warre that his aduersaries haue so tragically exaggerated, and yet (quoth he) how can it be called a warre seeing that it was done by the consent of the presidents, and that by couenant after periurie, wherewith both other gods and also Caesars name was violated. It now (quoth he) remaineth that I speake something concerning  the captiues. There were fortie theeues of Trachon, and afterward more that fled from Herode for feare of punishment, and fled vnto Arabia, whom Syllaeus protected and succoured

