It now (quoth he) remaineth that I speake something concerning  the captiues. There were fortie theeues of Trachon, and afterward more that fled from Herode for feare of punishment, and fled vnto Arabia, whom Syllaeus protected and succoured

to the iniurie of all men, and gaue them ground to inhabite, and was partaker of their praies;  
